@startuml
title Wildlife Monitor — Target capture and inference integration contracts
hide methods
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

class CaptureMetadata <<planned>> {
  +eventId: UUID
  +deploymentId: UUID
  +capturedAt: DateTime
}

class RawCaptureMessage <<planned>> {
  +eventId: UUID
  +deploymentId: UUID
  +capturedAt: DateTime
  +imageKey: String
}

class ClassifiedResultMessage <<planned>> {
  +eventId: UUID
  +deploymentId: UUID
  +capturedAt: DateTime
  +classificationStatus: ClassificationStatus
  +speciesLabel: String?
  +confidence: Float?
  +imageKey: String
  +modelVersion: String
  +classifiedAt: DateTime
}

enum ClassificationStatus {
  IDENTIFIED
  UNKNOWN
  NO_ANIMAL
}

interface PrivateObjectStorage {
  +put(image): imageKey
  +getTemporaryUrl(imageKey): URL
}

class CaptureIngestionAPI <<planned>>
class RabbitMQ <<broker>>
class AIInferenceWorker <<external service>>
class DetectionConsumer <<planned>>
class Detection <<domain record>> {
  +eventId: UUID <<unique>>
  +deploymentId: UUID
  +capturedAt: DateTime
  +classificationStatus: ClassificationStatus
  +imageKey: String?
  +classifiedAt: DateTime
}

CaptureIngestionAPI ..> CaptureMetadata : accepts multipart request
CaptureIngestionAPI ..> PrivateObjectStorage : saves image
CaptureIngestionAPI ..> RawCaptureMessage : publishes
RawCaptureMessage ..> RabbitMQ : captures.raw
RabbitMQ ..> AIInferenceWorker : consumes with bounded prefetch
AIInferenceWorker ..> ClassifiedResultMessage : publishes
ClassifiedResultMessage ..> RabbitMQ : detections.classified
RabbitMQ ..> DetectionConsumer : consumes
DetectionConsumer ..> Detection : validates and persists
Detection ..> PrivateObjectStorage : imageKey resolves privately

note right of Detection
  Planned behavior: immutable record;
  matching eventId retries return the prior row;
  conflicting eventId reuse is rejected.
end note

note bottom of RabbitMQ
  Persistent messages, bounded worker prefetch,
  and dead-letter handling are described in
  docs/api-contract.md and docs/architecture.md.
end note
@enduml
